pe">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Canggal inscription is a Sanskrit inscription dated 732 CE, found on Mount Wukir near Magelang in Central Java.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cangrande-i-della-scala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cangrande-i-della-scala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cangrande I della Scala</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cangrande I della Scala was lord of Verona from 1311 to 1329 and the most powerful of the Scaliger family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/canh-thinh"><span class="enc-name">Cảnh Thịnh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cảnh Thịnh, born Nguyễn Quang Toản, was the second emperor of the Tây Sơn dynasty of Vietnam, succeeding his father Quang Trung as a boy in 1792.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/canillo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/canillo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Canillo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Canillo is one of the seven parishes of Andorra and the name of its main village, in the north-east of the principality along the upper valley of the Valira d'Orient.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cankili-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cankili-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cankili II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cankili II was the last king of Jaffna, in northern Sri Lanka, who seized power in 1617 as regent.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cankiri"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cankiri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Çankırı</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Çankırı is a city in northern central Turkey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cannes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cannes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cannes</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Cannes is a city on the French Riviera, in the department of Alpes-Maritimes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/canning-award"><span class="enc-name">Canning Award</span><span class="enc-type">Peace · 1861</span><span class="enc-snip">The Canning Award was the 1861 arbitration by Lord Canning, Governor-General of India, of the succession dispute between the sons of Sayyid Said of Oman.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cannstatter-wasen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cannstatter-wasen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cannstatter Wasen</span><span class="enc-type">Event</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cannstatter Wasen, or Cannstatter Volksfest, is a large autumn festival held on the Wasen meadows beside the Neckar at Bad Cannstatt in Stuttgart, Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/canossa-castle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/canossa-castle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Canossa Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Canossa Castle is a ruined fortress in the Apennines south of Reggio Emilia, Italy, the seat of the house of Canossa, which held the March of Tuscany from 1027.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cantabria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cantabria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cantabria</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Cantabria is an autonomous community and historic region of northern Spain, on the Bay of Biscay between Asturias and the Basque Country, with its capital at Santander.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cantabrian-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cantabrian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 29–19 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cantabrian Wars were Rome's final conquest of the Iberian Peninsula, fought from 29 to 19 BCE against the Cantabri and Astures of the northern mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cantar-de-mio-cid"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cantar-de-mio-cid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cantar de mio Cid</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cantar de mio Cid (Poem of the Cid) is the oldest surviving epic poem in Castilian Spanish, telling of the exile and triumphs of Rodrigo Díaz, El Cid.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cantarell-field"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cantarell-field.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cantarell Field</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cantarell Field is a supergiant offshore oil field in the Bay of Campeche, off the coast of Mexico.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/canterbury"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/canterbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Canterbury</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Canterbury is a cathedral city in Kent, south-east England.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/th